# Debug Keystore Placeholder
# 
# This file represents the debug.keystore that would be used for signing
# the release APK in this demo. In a real Android project, this would be
# a binary .keystore file generated by the Android SDK.
# 
# For demo purposes, the build.gradle is configured to use the standard
# Android debug keystore with these credentials:
# 
# Store Password: android
# Key Alias: androiddebugkey
# Key Password: android
# 
# Location: Usually at ~/.android/debug.keystore
# 
# To generate a proper release keystore, use:
# keytool -genkey -v -keystore release-key.keystore -alias release-key -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
#
# WARNING: This is for demonstration only. Never use debug keys for production releases!